# The disk of create-partitions: every way of not changing it. FDISK
# refuses a choice not on the menu, to delete the primary partition while
# there is an extended one, or the extended partition while it has logical
# drives, and to create a second primary or extended partition, or a
# logical drive with no space left; the default answer to "Are you sure"
# before deleting a logical drive is No. FDISK then exits without
# restarting, and the disk is as it was.
disk 21411840 615/4/17
sectors ../create-partitions/expect.sectors
unchanged
wait A:\\>
type FDISK
key ret
wait Enter choice
key 9 ret
screen bad-choice
key 3 ret
wait Enter choice
key 1 ret
screen primary-refused
key esc
wait Enter choice
key 3 ret
wait Enter choice
key 2 ret
screen extended-refused
key esc
wait Enter choice
key 3 ret
wait Enter choice
key 3 ret
wait What drive
key shift-e ret
wait Volume Label
key ret
wait Are you sure
key ret
screen logical-kept
key esc
wait Enter choice
key 1 ret
wait Enter choice
key 1 ret
screen primary-exists
key esc
wait Enter choice
key 1 ret
wait Enter choice
key 2 ret
screen extended-exists
key esc
wait Enter choice
key 1 ret
wait Enter choice
key 3 ret
screen no-space
key esc
wait Enter choice
key 2 ret
screen already-active
key esc
screen menu
key esc
wait A:\\>
quit
